{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MkBc4BFUrCmUtWXNM3CFNS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BrBVhVC51yBg6Sz2Ht5fBW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","subagent_type":"Plan","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue paper review. Your focus is **novelty and related work**. Provide a detailed assessment. Do NOT assign a final score — that happens in the roundtable.\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"Hidden States Universally Encode Safety Commitment Better Than Text: A Cross-Architecture Evaluation of Reasoning Model Monitoring\"\n\nThe paper studies \"self-jailbreak\" in reasoning models where extended CoT reasoning culminates in a \"commitment point\" (CP). It compares hidden-state probes, text-based monitors, and unsupervised geometric methods across 4 models (r1-8b Llama, r1-32b Qwen2.5, QwQ-32B Qwen2.5, OpenThinker-7B Qwen2.5).\n\nThree claims: (1) HS temporal probes achieve pre-CP FPR 14–16% vs 27–36% text (pooled p=0.003), (2) Temporal context W=15 universally improves coverage +5–7pp, (3) Pre-textual detection fundamentally unreliable (median lead=0). Additional: cross-model transfer 67–74% accuracy.\n\n## Related Work Citations (14 total)\n1. DeepSeek-AI 2025 (DeepSeek-R1)\n2. Qwen 2025 (QwQ)\n3. Zhang et al. 2024 (HarmThoughts) - data source\n4. Li et al. 2024 (Self-Jailbreaking) - phenomenon\n5. Wang et al. 2024 (TrajGuard) - baseline\n6. Chen et al. 2024 (SafeSwitch)\n7. Liu et al. 2024 (SIREN)\n8. Zou et al. 2024 (Representation Engineering)\n9. Arditi et al. 2024 (Refusal directions)\n10. Adams & MacKay 2007 (BOCPD)\n11. Page 1954 (CUSUM)\n12. Lightman et al. 2023 (PRMs)\n13. Xie et al. 2025 (SafeRemind)\n14. Wu et al. 2025 (SafeThink)\n\nRelated Work has 3 subsections: Hidden-state safety detection, Reasoning model safety, Change-point detection.\n\n## Paper Structure\n10 pages: Intro (2pg), Related Work (1pg), Problem Setup (1pg), Methods (1pg), Experiments (2pg with 8 subsections), Ablations (1pg), Discussion (1pg), Conclusion (0.5pg), References (1pg), Appendix (1pg with CIs + 1 table).\n\n## Your Task\nEvaluate thoroughly on novelty and related work:\n\n1. **Novelty assessment**:\n   - Is studying CP detection in reasoning models genuinely novel?\n   - Is \"hidden states beat text\" surprising or expected from representation probing literature?\n   - Is cross-architecture transfer finding novel?\n   - Is \"pre-textual detection unreliable\" finding novel?\n   - How does this compare to probing classifiers literature (Belinkov, Conneau, etc.)?\n   - Empirical study vs methodological contribution?\n\n2. **Related work completeness**:\n   - Missing: probing classifiers (Belinkov, Conneau, Hewitt), activation patching/causal tracing (Meng et al.), steering vectors, latent space analysis, process supervision, circuit analysis, jailbreak detection literature?\n   - 14 citations sufficient for top venue?\n   - Positioning against prior art adequate?\n\n3. **Significance and impact**:\n   - Impact for safety community?\n   - \"Universal\" claim justified with 4 models (3 Qwen2.5-based)?\n   - Advances understanding or confirms expected?\n\n4. **Framing and positioning**:\n   - Title justified by evidence?\n   - Claims appropriately scoped?\n\n5. **Writing quality**:\n   - Well-written? Structural issues?\n   - AI writing markers (dashes, -ing phrases)?\n\nProvide: Strengths (bullet list), Weaknesses (bullet list), Questions for Authors (numbered), Preliminary tendency (lean accept/reject/borderline) with justification."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3720,"cache_read_input_tokens":62849,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3720},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"584eac82-aa50-4806-9859-0d2ba8093b1f","uuid":"61556e5a-c099-4183-99b3-510a1281c167"}
