{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPxZazSxjNNxAenMJjHaNJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tD2 PCA Visualization Results\n2\t============================\n3\t\n4\tTest set: 43 traces, 1835 steps (494 post-commit, 1341 pre-commit)\n5\t\n6\tLayer | Fisher(orig) | Fisher(PCA-3d) | Var Explained\n7\t------|-------------|----------------|---------------\n8\t  12  |    17.462   |     0.953      |    16.6%\n9\t  14  |    17.875   |     0.928      |    17.0%\n10\t  20  |    18.614   |     0.920      |    16.6%\n11\t  24  |    18.106   |     1.111      |    15.9%\n12\t\n13\tNotes:\n14\t- Fisher ratio in original 4096-dim space is high (~17-18) across all layers\n15\t- In PCA 3-component projection: ~0.9-1.1, confirming moderate but real separation\n16\t- Variance explained by top-3 PCs is low (16-17%), signal spread across many dimensions\n17\t- Layer 24 shows best PCA-space separability (1.111)\n18\t\n19\tConclusion: Signal EXISTS — separation visible in PCA but not dominant in top components.\n20\tThis explains why linear probes achieve 78-81% (D1) — the signal is real but distributed.\n21\t\n22\tFiles on server:\n23\t- /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/diagnostics/pca_layer12.png\n24\t- /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/diagnostics/pca_layer14.png\n25\t- /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/diagnostics/pca_layer20.png\n26\t- /root/autodl-tmp/contrastive_trace_safety/artifacts/diagnostics/pca_layer24.png"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BrBVhVC51yBg6Sz2Ht5fBW","session_id":"584eac82-aa50-4806-9859-0d2ba8093b1f","uuid":"60fabdd0-fc88-4be7-904d-33943818a036","timestamp":"2026-05-16T21:53:46.274Z"}
